 "source": {
  "url": "https://kubernetes.io/releases/version-skew-policy/",
  "ref": "upstream Kubernetes version skew policy (kube-proxy section)",
  "lastVerified": "2026-08-29",
  "note": "supportWindows are DERIVED, not transcribed row-by-row: the policy states kube-proxy \"must not be newer than kube-apiserver\" and \"may be up to three minor versions older\" (two, for kube-proxy < 1.25). So for kube-proxy X: minK8s = X (never newer than the API server) and maxK8s = X + 3 (X + 2 below 1.25). This is an upstream Kubernetes rule and applies to every distribution, not just EKS. AddonCompatCatalogTest re-derives the arithmetic for every row so a hand-edit cannot silently widen a window."
 },
